# The plaintext credential store is GONE — replaced by the SOPS-encrypted,
# committed .github/instructions/secrets.enc.yaml. This line stays as a guard so
# a plaintext secrets.yml can never be committed if one is ever recreated (e.g.
# by an old runbook or a `sops -d` redirect). It does NOT match secrets.enc.yaml.
secrets.yml
# Glob form, not `.history/`: a directory-level ignore prunes the whole
# subtree before git ever evaluates the negations below, so `!.history/*.md`
# would be silently dead (git can't re-include a file whose parent dir is
# excluded). Keep this as `.history/*` or the negations stop working again.
.history/*
.torrent-cache
*.log
# Negate the intentionally-tracked files by EXACT NAME, not by `*.md`/`*.sh`
# glob (#591). This directory holds raw operator command logs - real IPs,
# hostnames, full command output, written under a "git-ignored so it's safe"
# assumption (.history/README.md) - and this repo is public. A glob negation
# means a plain `git add -A` stages every new log; there were 21 untracked
# ones when #591 was swept. Tracking here is opt-in per file, so anything
# new stays local unless someone negates it by name. A write-up that
# really belongs in git goes to docs/ or .github/instructions/, not here.
!.history/README.md
!.history/USAGE.md
!.history/log-cmd.sh
!.history/shell-functions.sh
!.history/start-logged-session.sh
!.history/2026-05-17-wg-hop-lxc-setup.md
!.history/2026-05-17-wg-hop-public-exposure.md
raid-migration
.claude/

# Retired agent scaffolding, archived to ~/.a5c-archive-epaflix on 2026-08-23.
# The rule stays as a guard so the tree can never come back (cf. secrets.yml).
.a5c/

# Sensitive data - database dumps, backups, research extracts with credentials
2-k3s/08.servarr/_backups/postgres-dumps/
2-k3s/08.servarr/_backups/sqlite-zips/
2-k3s/08.servarr/_backups/postgres-schemas-*/
2-k3s/08.servarr/research/app-configs.xml
2-k3s/08.servarr/research/truenas-configs.txt
2-k3s/08.servarr/research/truenas-ix-apps-full.txt
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.zip
# ...but the lingarr boot guard is SOURCE, not a dump: public SQL with no
# credentials, mounted as a ConfigMap by `2-k3s/08.servarr/kustomization.yaml`
# (#870). Without this negation the `*.sql` rule above silently drops it, the
# `configMapGenerator` has no file to read, and ArgoCD fails to render the
# servarr Application. Scoped to that one directory on purpose - database dumps
# stay ignored everywhere else.
!2-k3s/08.servarr/lingarr/files/*.sql

# Local cache from kustomize+helm pull (per-Application 2-k3s/0X.*/charts/)
charts/

# SOPS plaintext drafts — never commit. Always encrypt to *.enc.yaml first.
*-plaintext.yaml
*.plaintext.yaml

# Superpowers subagent-driven-development scratch (ledger, briefs, review packages).
# Per-plan workspaces under .superpowers/sdd/<plan>/ — the git history is the record.
.superpowers/

# Compose .env files hold runtime secrets (AirVPN account password, Cloudflare
# tunnel tokens) for the user-VM stacks. Never commit these.
.env
*.env
!*.env.example
# Version pins, no secrets; Renovate and the t3code guest both read it from git.
!2-k3s/13.t3code/versions.env

# Playwright MCP scratch - browser snapshots, which can capture account pages.
.playwright-mcp/

# Python bytecode. images/vpn-picker/ is the repo's only Python source; running
# its selftest locally drops a __pycache__ next to it.
__pycache__/

# Scratch triage notes (#662) - per-issue investigation notes and baseline/
# before-state captures written while working an issue. Unlike .history/,
# NO tracked exceptions: the GitHub issue/PR they feed is the durable record,
# and at least one baseline capture already carried a raw show title (banned
# per this repo's rule on media names in committed git). Convention documented
# in general.instructions.md.
artifacts/

# Local backups. CLAUDE.md has always described this as git-ignored; it was not.
# Found while taking a pre-decommission copy of filebrowser's database, which
# contains OIDC client secrets and password hashes.
/backups/

# Homelab-only kubeconfig generated by .github/hooks/install-kubeconfig-epaflix.sh
# (#856). `kubectl config view --flatten` embeds client-certificate-data and
# client-key-data, so this file holds live cluster credentials - never commit
# it. Being ignored also enlists check-no-force-added-ignored.sh (blocks
# `git add -f`) and the ci.yml "No tracked file matches .gitignore" step.
/.kube/

# jellyseerr/seerr config backups. These carried 8 LIVE secrets (an Authentik
# OIDC client secret, seerr api key, vapid private key, 3 *arr api keys) into
# git history for ~6 months (#730). Untracking stops further copies; it does
# NOT remove them from history - rotation is the remedy.
2-k3s/08.servarr/jellyseerr/backups/
